4.2 STATE ISOLATION RULE

World state MUST NOT directly mutate GRID state.
All external effects MUST pass through GNPL events.


---

5. EXECUTION LOOP (WORLD TICK ENGINE)

Each world runs independently:

WORLD TICK:

1. ingest portal events (incoming GNPL)
2. validate via AEGIS (local + global mirror)
3. route actions (ODIN-local)
4. execute logic (SKADI-local)
5. update local graph state
6. run internal consensus (mini GNPL)
7. emit outbound events (to GRID via portal)
8. log to Supabase (if permitted)
9. checkpoint to GitHub (if marked persistent)


---

6. AGENT HOSTING MODEL

6.1 AGENTS INSIDE WORLD

Agent = executable node-bound process within world kernel

Each agent has:

Field	Function

role	purpose
scope	allowed graph region
memory	local state buffer
permissions	edge/node mutation rights
constraints	AEGIS ruleset



---

6.2 AGENT TYPES

Type	Function

worker	performs tasks
planner	generates internal routing
observer	monitors state
stabilizer	reduces entropy
simulator	runs predictive models



---

7. PORTAL SYSTEM (WORLD ↔ GRID)

7.1 PORTAL DEFINITION

PORTAL = controlled boundary edge between WORLD and GRID


---

7.2 PORTAL RULES

all inbound data must be GNPL validated

all outbound changes must be event-based

no direct memory writes allowed

all cross-world interaction is asynchronous



---

7.3 PORTAL TYPES

Type	Function

input portal	receives events
output portal	emits state changes
memory portal	syncs snapshots
execution portal	triggers external actions



---

8. WORLD CONSENSUS SYSTEM (LOCAL GNPL)

Each world runs a mini consensus engine:

LOCAL CONSENSUS = resolve internal conflicts before GRID sync

Uses same principles as Patch 29:

scoring

conflict resolution

merge/split/prune logic



---

9. CONSISTENCY GUARANTEE MODEL

9.1 GLOBAL CONSISTENCY RULE

GRID state = sum(all validated world outputs)

But:

worlds are not allowed to directly assume GRID truth

they only react to propagated snapshots



---

9.2 DRIFT CONTROL

Handled by:

System	Role

HUGINN	cross-world reconciliation
HALO	structural validation
NEMESIS	duplicate world detection
LOKI	rollback of corrupted world states



---

10. TICK SYNCHRONIZATION (KRONOS)

Worlds can operate:

Mode	Behavior

synced	aligned global ticks
async	independent time flow
burst	high-frequency local updates
frozen	paused state snapshot



